//   playback CAP. 1.0 = as fast as live. 0.5 matches the old playback
//   (which ran at half live rate). The slowest-limited axis in a move
//   runs at exactly this; the rest run slower to arrive together.
const float PLAY_SPEED = 0.8;

// Seconds spent accelerating at the start and decelerating at the end
// of EVERY move, regardless of distance. Short moves keep the same
// accel/decel times and simply reach a lower peak speed - the shape
// stays identical, which is what makes a routine look consistent.
// Raise for lazier, more cinematic motion; lower for snappier.
const float PLAY_ACCEL_TIME_S = 0.35;
const float PLAY_DECEL_TIME_S = 0.45;

